---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import TransportPlanner from '../../components/TransportPlanner.astro';
import WorkshopLinks from '../../components/WorkshopLinks.astro';
import art from '../../assets/projects/transport.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout title="Automated Public Transport Planning" description="A Cities: Skylines 1 Development prototype for bus route proposals and confirmed creation attempts. Game acceptance is pending." path="automated-public-transport-planning/" active="mods">
	<section class="hero page-wrap">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Mod 02 · Development prototype</p>
			<h1>Automated Public Transport Planning</h1>
			<p class="hero-lead">The Development prototype can preview proposed bus lines and attempt to create a selected route after you arm the feature and confirm. It also offers an existing-line stop-move prototype. These attempts may change a save, and runnable routes are not guaranteed.</p>
			<div class="status-strip"><span class="tag">May change saves</span><span class="tag">Confirmation required</span><span class="tag">Game acceptance pending</span></div>
			<WorkshopLinks mod="transport" />
		</div>
		<figure class="hero-art"><Image src={art} alt="Automated Public Transport Planning artwork" widths={[560, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 45vw" format="webp" quality={78} loading="eager" /><figcaption class="art-note">Project artwork · not a gameplay screenshot</figcaption></figure>
	</section>

	<nav class="subnav page-wrap" aria-label="Transport planning guide"><a href={base + 'wiki/transport/overview/'}>Guide</a><a href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Roadmap</a></nav>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">Diagnostics and planning</p>
				<h2>Survey, preview and review.</h2>
				<p>The mod can survey roads, stops and the transit network. These survey diagnostics do not create routes; the separate Development route-creation prototype can change the city after confirmation. Diagnostics results are written to the game log:</p>
				<ul class="feature-list">
					<li><strong>Measure planning costs</strong><span>How long planning work would take on your city (a brief pause).</span></li>
					<li><strong>Capture a world snapshot</strong><span>A summary of the roads and stops the planner would use.</span></li>
					<li><strong>Build the route graph</strong><span>The network of possible stop connections.</span></li>
				</ul>
				<p lang="en">The historical stop-move prototype requires preview, enabling the feature, and two confirmations before an attempt. Attempts may affect saves; back up and use a separate test city. Game and save/reload acceptance remain pending.</p>
				<details>
					<summary lang="en">Historical prototype release record - not a current mod download</summary>
				<p>The <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/releases/tag/Automated_Public_Transport_Planning-dev-41252417067-1">historical Development release</a> from <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/commit/60976d7c34f73aee698af192a660abe001ec347d">source 60976d7</a> included manual and automatic move-only editing for existing regular city-bus lines with 3–6 stops, intended to retain the line ID and stop count. Preview, enable and confirm twice before attempting a change. Both original and target stops must use exact RoadAI and pass segment-eligibility and placement checks. Stops on bridges, tunnels, station roads or unknown/custom-AI roads are conservatively rejected.</p>
				</details>
				{false && (
				<p lang="en"><strong>Distribution update, 3 November 2026:</strong> GitHub Releases is planned for the Dev Manager Windows Setup.exe, while mods are intended to come from separate artifact branches. The installer is not built or published. The AI Improve and Automated Public Transport Planning branch candidates remain local and are not committed, pushed, or published. The earlier release-attachment guidance below is historical.</p>
				)}
				<p lang="en"><strong>Distribution:</strong> If Dev Manager's Windows Setup.exe has been published, check <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/releases">GitHub Releases</a>. The planned app is intended to show verified module builds when available; availability varies by module. Earlier module-release guidance on this page is historical.</p>
				<!-- Notice wording: OpenAI-Codex_distribution_components. -->
				<details>
					<summary lang="en">Historical release check - not a current mod download</summary>
				<p>Availability check, 2 November 2026: current installable attachments could not be verified. Check <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/releases">GitHub Releases</a> and the actual release attachments before installing; automatically generated source archives are not installable mod files.</p>
				</details>
				<p>Back up saves and use a separate test city. Recovery is non-atomic and may fail; passengers, vehicles and paths may not be fully restored. In-game operation and save/reload have not been accepted.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="screenshot-stack">
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Diagnostics in the mod options" description="The language selector and the Diagnostics buttons on the mod’s options page." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Survey results in the log" description="The summary written to the game log after a city loads or a diagnostic runs." />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- Browser illustration is not an in-game screenshot. OpenAI-Codex_Responsible: Modpack_Website. -->
	<section class="interactive-section"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="section-label">Planning concept · browser demo</p><h2>From demand to a bus line you approve.</h2><TransportPlanner locale="en" /></div></section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack"><p class="eyebrow">Roadmap</p><h2>One step at a time.</h2><p>The Development prototype is experimental and can damage saves. Back up before testing and confirm each creation attempt.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Full roadmap →</a></div>
			<div class="roadmap"><article><strong>Survey</strong><p>Read-only network survey and diagnostics.</p></article><article><strong>Preview</strong><p>Development proposals estimate candidate bus routes.</p></article><article><strong>Attempt creation</strong><p>Arm the feature and confirm a selected proposal. Game acceptance remains pending.</p></article></div>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
